You may write plugins for SERN and share or sell them under any terms you choose. The plugin documentation, type definitions and examples we publish may be used, copied and adapted for that purpose. A plugin is yours; SERN itself stays under this agreement.

4. Your data

SERN works on your computer and your repositories. Features you turn on, such as sign-in to Git hosting services, AI features, plugins and update checks, connect to the services they name. Your code and data remain yours.

